# HOME_START + OPENING_OFFICE: text keys and flags the code reads

Owner: Coder (home_start). Status: DEV, Oct 23 2026, nothing committed.
Text Bot owns `text/overworld_lines.json` and `text/*.py`. The code never writes them; it reads them at runtime.
Until a key is merged, the code uses its fallback. Fallbacks are the HOME_START_v1 / OPENING_OFFICE_v1 drafts.
A brand-new key with no draft yet shows a `[TODO Text Bot: <key>]` prefix in game, so you can see it in shots.

## Page format
- Normal entries use the usual shape: `lines` plus optional `v_<flag>` variants, picked with the same `pick()` as every other NPC.
- In a multi-speaker scene, a page may start with `WHO: text`. WHO can be MANAGER, RON, LAB TECH or PLAYER.
  The code also accepts `{ "speaker": "...", "text": "..." }`.
  A page with no tag uses the default speaker for that entry.
- An inner thought has no tag and plays as italic text in a dashed box with no name.
  These keys play as thoughts: player_start, door_block, cradle_not_yet, test_run_logged and leave_block.
- Placeholders: `{lead}` (starter name), `{count}` (crystals), `{n}` and `{need}` (test-run progress). The usual textVars also work.

## Keys
| Key | When it plays | Status |
|---|---|---|
| maps.house_2f.player_start | Wake-up thought after the new-game fade-in | HOME_START_v1 |
| maps.house_1f.ron | Ron's morning briefing (default). Sets talked_ron_morning. Needs a short repeat variant `v_talked_ron_morning`, placed after `v_flg_promoted`. | HOME_START_v1 (+ repeat) |
| maps.house_1f.door_block | Thought when the front door is blocked before the briefing | HOME_START_v1 |
| maps.office_int.scene_promotion | Talking to the office manager on a new game. Sets flg_promoted, then fades to the lab. | OPENING_OFFICE_v1 |
| maps.office_int.manager_starter_repeat | Manager talked to again after the promotion but before a starter is picked | NEW placeholder |
| maps.lab_brookhollow.cradle_not_yet | Thought when a cradle is used before flg_promoted (new game only) | NEW placeholder |
| maps.lab_brookhollow.scene_starter_intro | First cradle use after the promotion. Plays once (seen key `intro:starter_intro`). | OPENING_OFFICE_v1 |
| maps.lab_brookhollow.starter_confirm | Yes/No question, `{lead}` = species | OPENING_OFFICE_v1 |
| maps.lab_brookhollow.scene_starter_after | After Yes (sets got_starter) | OPENING_OFFICE_v1 |
| maps.lab_brookhollow.scene_test_run | Straight after; sets test_run_started | OPENING_OFFICE_v1 |
| maps.lab_brookhollow.crystals_received | `{count}` dominance crystals given (5) | NEW placeholder |
| maps.lab_brookhollow.manager_test_run_repeat | Manager or researcher talked to during the run | OPENING_OFFICE_v1 |
| maps.lab_brookhollow.scene_test_run_return | Entering the lab with test_run_done | OPENING_OFFICE_v1 |
| maps.lab_brookhollow.scene_job_briefing | Straight after; sets job_briefed (pay is on progress) | OPENING_OFFICE_v1 |
| system_opening.test_run_progress | Toast `{n}/{need}` after each catch that gets logged | NEW placeholder |
| system_opening.test_run_logged | Thought when the 2nd catch is logged; sets test_run_done | NEW placeholder |
| system_opening.leave_block | Thought when an edge exit is blocked. One entry; use `v_` variants by stage (see below). | NEW placeholder |
| system_opening.free_roam | Toast after job_briefed | NEW placeholder |

Stages for leave_block variants:
- office: no flg_promoted yet. Base `lines`.
- lab: no got_starter yet. `v_flg_promoted`.
- run: during the test run, only route1 is allowed. `v_test_run_started`.
- back: run done, go back to the lab. `v_test_run_done`.

The code fallbacks already change by stage.

## Flags, all set by code
intro_new_game, talked_ron_morning, flg_promoted, got_starter (set by party.chooseStarter), test_run_started, test_run_done, job_briefed.

## Counters and constants
- Counters: test_run_base (baseline of owned + Kilindex-logged creatures at test_run_started) and test_run_logged.
- Test-run target: 2. Crystals given: 5 × `dominance_crystal`.
- Allowed area during the run: brookhollow and route1.

## Objectives (hard-coded strings; tell Coder if Text Bot wants them as keys)
1. Talk to Ron downstairs
2. Go to the Revival Tech office
3. Pick a partner at the lab
4. Test run: catch and log 2 wild Kilumen (n/2)
5. Return to the lab
6. (none: free roam)
